where the last equality follows from the induction hypothesis and the fact that $\binom{n}{k} + \binom{n}{k+1} = \binom{n+1}{k+1}$. Therefore, we have shown that $f(x, y) = f(x - 1, y + 1)$ for all $(x, y) \in \mathbb{Z}^2$.

