To maximize $F(a_1, \ldots, a_n)$, we should minimize $1 + a_1$. Since $\sum_{i=1}^n a_i = 1$, minimizing $1 + a_1$ is equivalent to maximizing $a_1$.

Given that $a_1 \geq a_2 \geq \cdots \geq a_n$, the maximum value of $a_1$ is $1 - \sum_{i=2}^n a_i$. Substituting this into the expression for $F(a_1, \ldots, a_n)$ gives:

$$
F(a_1, \ldots, a_n) = \frac{1 - \sum_{i=2}^n a_i + \sum_{i=1}^n a_i^2}{1 + 1 - \sum_{i=2}^n a_i} = \frac{1 + \sum_{i=1}^n a_i^2 - \sum_{i=2}^n a_i}{2 - \sum_{i=2}^n a_i}.
