Since $\sum_{i=1}^n a_i = 1$ and $a_i \geq 0$, the maximum value of $F(a_1, \ldots, a_n)$ occurs when $\sum_{i=2}^n a_i$ is minimized, which is $0$. In this case, $F(a_1, \ldots, a_n) = \frac{1 + \sum_{i=1}^n a_i^2}{2} = \frac{1 + 1}{2} = 1$.

However, since we are looking for the maximum value of the expression $\frac{\sum_{i=1}^n a_i(a_i + b_i)}{\sum_{i=1}^n b_i(a_i + b_i)}$, we need to find the maximum value of the numerator and denominator separately and then take their ratio.

The maximum value of the numerator is $a_1(a_1 + b_1) = a_1(a_1 + 1 - \sum_{i=2}^n b_i) = a_1 + a_1 - a_1 \sum_{i=2}^n b_i$, which is $n - \sum_{i=2}^n a_i$. The maximum value of the denominator is $b_1(a_1 + b_1) = (1 - \sum_{i=2}^n b_i)(a_1 + 1 - \sum_{i=2}^n b_i) = 1 - \sum_{i=2}^n b_i + a_1 - a_1 \sum_{i=2}^n b_i = 1 - \sum_{i=2}^n a_i$.

Taking the ratio of the maximum values of the numerator and denominator gives:

$$
\frac{(n - \sum_{i=2}^n a_i)}{(1 - \sum_{i=2}^n a_i)} = \frac{n - 1}{\sum_{i=2}^n a_i}.
