Therefore, \(f(x)\) must be either injective or constant. Since \(f(1)\) is a positive integer, the only possible solutions are:
1. \(f(x) = x\),
2. \(f(x) = \begin{cases} n & \text{if } x = 1 \\ 1 & \text{if } x > 1 \end{cases} \) for any \(n\),
