$$\frac{1}{2}(\sin x_1 + \sin x_2 + \sin x_3 - \sin y_1 - \sin y_2 - \sin y_3) = 0.$$

Since $\sin x_1$, $\sin x_2$, $\sin x_3$, $\sin y_1$, $\sin y_2$, and $\sin y_3$ are all non-zero (as they are the sines of acute angles), we have:

